Your problem isn't that you're missing the mysqli extension.

If you're doing something like this:

```
namespace Listener;

class Foo
{
    public function bar() {
        $conn = new mysqli(...);
    }
}
```

Then PHP will interpret
`new mysqli()`
 as
`new \Listener\mysqli()`
 because you're currently in the
`\Listener`
 namespace. To fix this, you can just explicitly anchor
`mysqli()`
 to the root namespace:

```
$conn = new \mysqli(...);
```

